</blockquote>
<p>Probably remove 'evidently' here, it makes the flow a bit odd, but that's a personal thing.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>a catastrophic loss of mental capacity</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Tone 'catastrophic'.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>only rudimentary grunting</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Bad tone with 'only'. I don't know if 'rudimentary grunting' is appropriate term for the phrase, but I don't know what the appropriate term would be.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>subjects are invariable in a state of violent panic</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Could possibly be reworded as 'affected persons invariably enter a highly unpredictable panic state' or something like that.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>hitherto-undiscovered</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I would consider hitherto to be bad tone.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>proved fruitless</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Again.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>radical simplification of subject's brain structures</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You didn't mention this in the transformation. Consistencyplease.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>we'll all finally be cool.</p>
</blockquote>
